{"id":"u-5739802e-4165-48c3-b369-460a03e04050","src":"community","title":"Oxline Strength","author":"Kurtis H.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/t8130l-oxline-strength","desc":"Oxline Strength is a hybrid performance program built to develop real-world strength, explosive power, athletic conditioning, and a dense sleeper-build physique without excessive bodybuilding volume or constant max-effort lifting.\n\nThe program combines:\n\nheavy compound strength work,\nexplosive power training,\nloaded carries,\nrotational core work,\nVO2 max conditioning,\nand athletic movement\n\nto build a body that is:\n\nstrong,\ndurable,\nexplosive,\nwell-conditioned,\nand capable outside the gym.\n\nPrimary strength development is focused through:\n\nBench Press\n(1RM focus)\nTrap Bar Deadlift\n(6RM focus)\nBarbell Hack Squat\n(6RM focus)\n\nwhile supplemental work improves:\n\nbracing,\nupper-back density,\ngrip strength,\nrotational force production,\nand athletic explosiveness.\n\nThe system is designed for long-term progression and sustainability, making it ideal for lifters who:\n\nwant to become very strong without looking oversized,\nparticipate in sports or conditioning outside the gym,\nvalue durability and recovery,\nor want better transfer into combat sports and athletic performance.\nKey Things to Know Before Starting\nAll percentages are based on 90% of your estimated 1 rep max for all main lifts.\nMain lifts use percentage-based progression combined with RPE autoregulation.\nMost training should stay around RPE 7–8.\nExplosive intent matters on every rep.\nAccessories stay relatively consistent while main lifts progress weekly.\nWeek 8 is a mandatory deload.\nVO2 max conditioning should be performed on Tuesdays after upper-body training.\nPlaying a sport weekly is strongly encouraged for athletic carryover and conditioning.\nAim for 8–12k steps daily to improve recovery, conditioning, and body composition.\nConditioning should improve performance, not destroy recovery.\nRecovery quality will determine progress:\nsleep,\nhydration,\nelectrolytes,\nprotein,\nand walking matter.\n\nThis program rewards:\n\nconsistency,\ndiscipline,\nexplosiveness,\nand intelligent effort\n\nfar more than grinding yourself into the floor.","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-09-08T02:19:08.248Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Box Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"r":6,"pct":72,"x":4}],"note":"RPE 7-7.5"},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Farmer's Walk (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":30,"rpe":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Copenhagen Plank","sets":[{"sec":30,"rpe":7,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":5}],"note":"RPE 7.5"},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":7.5},{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Broad Jump","sets":[{"r":2,"rpe":6,"x":4}],"note":"Explode. Rest longer if quality drops"},{"n":"Trap Bar Deadlift","sets":[{"r":6,"pct":72,"x":4}],"note":"RPE 7-7.5\nFast lockout. No ugly reps"},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":4}],"note":"Power pulls through torso. No cheating"},{"n":"Suitcase Carry","sets":[{"r":30,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Neutral spine. Obliques and grip should be working hard"},{"n":"Landmine Twist","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Explosive but controlled"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70,"x":3}],"note":"RPE 6.5-7"},{"n":"Zercher Bulgarian Split Squat","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Back Extension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Pre